pos/free5gc/smf/tags","blobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/git/blobs{/sha}","git_tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/git/tags{/sha}","git_refs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/git/refs{/sha}","trees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/git/trees{/sha}","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/statuses/{sha}","languages_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/languages","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/stargazers","contributors_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/deployments","created_at":"2020-04-26T19:53:06Z","updated_at":"2026-11-05T07:50:57Z","pushed_at":"2026-11-05T07:50:51Z","git_url":"git://github.com/free5gc/smf.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:free5gc/smf.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/free5gc/smf.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/free5gc/smf","homepage":null,"size":11257,"stargazers_count":26,"watchers_count":26,"language":"Go","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":142,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":14,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":142,"open_issues":14,"watchers":26,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/pulls/246","html_url":"https://github.com/free5gc/smf/pull/246","diff_url":"https://github.com/free5gc/smf/pull/246.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/free5gc/smf/pull/246.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Summary\r\n\r\n`sendPDUSessionEstablishmentAccept` returns early without cleanup when it fails to build the N1 message, fails to build the N2 message, or cannot get the namf-comm access token. By then the AMF already has the 201 and the PFCP session is installed on the UPF. The SM context stays in `ActivePending` with its UE IP, TEIDs, UPF rule IDs, SM policy association and SDM subscription allocated, and nothing releases it. This is the accept-side case from free5gc/free5gc#1177. The reject side was fixed in #236.\r\n\r\n## Fix\r\n\r\n**Before `N1N2MessageTransfer` is invoked** (N1 build, N2 build, access token), the failed establishment is always released. The Accept has not been sent, so there is no doubt about delivery. `releaseFailedEstablishment` deletes the PFCP sessions through `ReleaseTunnel`, then calls `RemoveSMContextFromAllNF(smContext, true)`, so the AMF is notified and local resources are freed. This mirrors the reject path. The local release still happens if PFCP Session Deletion fails, which avoids the #1179 pattern.\r\n\r\n**After `N1N2MessageTransfer` is invoked**, the SM context is released only when the AMF returns 403 with cause `INVALID_SM_CONTEXT`. TS 29.518 clause 5.2.2.3.1.2:\r\n\r\n> The NF service consumer (i.e. the SMF) that receives this application error shall remove the SM Context for the PDU session and release the PDU session resource in (H-)SMF if available. The SMF shall not send a SMContextStatusNotification to the AMF for the PDU session release.\r\n\r\nSo this path uses `sendNotification = false`.\r\n\r\nTransport and decoding errors, and other N1N2 application errors, do not show whether the AMF processed the request. They keep the existing behaviour. `N1_MSG_NOT_TRANSFERRED` is a 200 OK cause, so the session becomes `Active` as before.\r\n\r\nLocking matches the reject path. `ReleaseTunnel` doesn't take `SMLock`, and the final removal waits for the lock on its own goroutine.\r\n\r\n## Tests\r\n\r\n`internal/sbi/processor/datapath_accept_test.go` runs through the real create handler and establishment goroutine:\r\n\r\n- AMF access token failure: SM context released, PFCP deletion sent, N1N2 not sent\r\n- `INVALID_SM_CONTEXT`: SM context released, PFCP deletion sent, SM policy terminated, no `SMContextStatusNotification`\r\n- `INVALID_SM_CONTEXT` with PFCP deletion failure: local release still happens\r\n- Success: session kept\r\n- No release, table-driven: `N1_MSG_NOT_TRANSFERRED`, transport error, undecodable response, 500 `SYSTEM_FAILURE`, 403 `UE_IN_NON_ALLOWED_AREA`, 504 `UE_NOT_REACHABLE`\r\n\r\nOn `main`, the three release tests fail. The no-release cases pass there, because they keep main's behaviour.\r\n\r\n`go test ./...` passes, `-race` is clean on the touched packages, and golangci-lint shows no new issues.\r\n\r\n## Out of scope\r\n\r\n- Releasing on N1N2 failures where the spec doesn't require it (AMF unreachable, other 4xx/5xx). The SM context still stays in `ActivePending` there, as on `main`.\r\n- Setting `nfId` in the `N1MessageContainer`. The AMF returns `INVALID_SM_CONTEXT` only when the request's `nfId` names a different SMF (TS 29.518 clause 5.2.2.3.1.2), and the SMF doesn't send it yet.\r\n- Releasing the CHF charging session (free5gc/free5gc#1180, #1186)\r\n- An existing narrow race where a concurrent AMF release could run `ReleaseTunnel` twice; the same pattern exists on other release paths\r\n\r\nRelated: free5gc/free5gc#1177, #236","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/issues/246/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/issues/246/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"actor":{"login":"maringantis","id":27370703,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MzcwNzAz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27370703?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maringantis","html_url":"https://github.com/maringantis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maringantis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maringantis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maringantis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maringantis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maringantis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maringantis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maringantis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maringantis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.co