","git_tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/git/tags{/sha}","git_refs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/git/refs{/sha}","trees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/git/trees{/sha}","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/statuses/{sha}","languages_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/languages","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/stargazers","contributors_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/deployments","created_at":"2020-04-26T19:53:06Z","updated_at":"2026-11-05T07:50:57Z","pushed_at":"2026-11-05T07:50:51Z","git_url":"git://github.com/free5gc/smf.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:free5gc/smf.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/free5gc/smf.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/free5gc/smf","homepage":null,"size":11257,"stargazers_count":26,"watchers_count":26,"language":"Go","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":142,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":14,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":142,"open_issues":14,"watchers":26,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/pulls/247","html_url":"https://github.com/free5gc/smf/pull/247","diff_url":"https://github.com/free5gc/smf/pull/247.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/free5gc/smf/pull/247.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Summary\r\n\r\nAdds SMF business metrics, following the pattern of the AMF's `internal/metrics/business` package and the shared `github.com/free5gc/util/metrics` package. They cover PDU session establishment and release outcomes, the SM contexts the SMF currently holds, and PFCP requests to UPFs (result and latency).\r\n\r\nThe SMF already exports generic SBI metrics. They show that an SM context request failed, but not why, what happened after the 201 (PFCP, N1N2 transfer of the Accept), or whether SM contexts are leaking. These metrics fill that gap and make the leak reports in free5gc/free5gc#1176-#1180 measurable.\r\n\r\n## Metrics\r\n\r\nAll names use the configured `metrics.namespace` (default `free5gc`) and the `smf_business` subsystem.\r\n\r\n| Metric | Type | Labels | Recorded in |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| `free5gc_smf_business_pdu_session_establishment_total` | counter | `status` (successful/failure), `cause` | Every end of the establishment procedure: early rejects, `makeEstRejectResAndReleaseSMContext`, `EstHandler` (PFCP failure), `sendPDUSessionEstablishmentAccept` |\r\n| `free5gc_smf_business_pdu_session_release_total` | counter | `trigger`, `status`, `cause` | `releaseSession` (shared by UE, AMF, duplicate-ID and local duplicate releases) |\r\n| `free5gc_smf_business_pdu_session_current_count` | gauge | `state` | Computed at scrape time by counting the SM context pool |\r\n| `free5gc_smf_business_pfcp_request_total` | counter | `message_type`, `upf`, `result` (success/rejected/timeout/error) | `PfcpServer.sendRequest`, the single path for SMF→UPF requests |\r\n| `free5gc_smf_business_pfcp_request_duration_seconds` | histogram | `message_type`, `upf` | Same place, observed only when a response arrived |\r\n\r\n**Cardinality:** every label value comes from a constant in code or from the operator's config. There are no SUPI, IMSI or other per-subscriber labels. Establishment causes reuse the 3GPP cause the SMF already returns (from `pkg/errors`), plus five SMF-defined causes for failures with no 3GPP cause (for example, after the 201 has been sent). `upf` is the node ID (IP) of a UPF from `userplaneInformation`, so it has one value per configured UPF.\r\n\r\n**Active sessions:** I didn't use a gauge maintained with Inc/Dec, because it would drift on exactly the code paths that leak. `pdu_session_current_count` counts the SM context pool on each scrape, so it always matches what the SMF holds. Active sessions are `state=\"Active\"`.\r\n\r\n**When disabled:** nothing is registered, and every recording function returns after the same two boolean checks the AMF uses. The PFCP send path skips the timing entirely.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\n- `internal/metrics/business/`: new package (`types.go`, `pdu_session.go`, `pfcp.go`) mirroring the AMF's layout.\r\n- `pkg/service/init.go`: `getCustomMetrics()` registers the collectors when `metrics.enable` is true (same function as the AMF's).\r\n- `internal/pfcp/`: `sendRequest` now wraps the original (renamed `sendRequestAndWait`) to record the result and latency. The timeout error wraps a sentinel so `errors.Is` can detect it. The message text is unchanged.\r\n- `internal/context/sm_context.go`: `CountSMContextsByState()` for the scrape-time gauge.\r\n- `internal/sbi/processor/`: recording calls at the establishment outcome points; `releaseSession` takes a trigger and records the outcome (the old body is now `releasePfcpSessions`, unchanged).\r\n- `go.mod`: adds `github.com/kylelemons/godebug` as an indirect dependency. It's required by `prometheus/testutil` in the tests, and `go.sum` already had it.\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n\r\n- `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...` and `gofmt` are clean.\r\n- `go test ./...`: 263 passed, 0 failed (main: 241). 22 new tests and subtests cover:\r\n  - `business`: collector names in a real registry, each counter, the scrape-time gauge following the pool, histogram buckets (a timeout is counted but not observed), and recording as a no-op with nil collectors when disabled.\r\n  - `pfcp`: message type and result classification (timeout through error wrapping, rejected, missing Cause, wrong response type, heartbeat), and an end-to-end heartbeat through the real PFCP server for both success and timeout.\r\n  - `processor`: `HandlePDUSessionSMContextCreate` records the right cause for N1 error, missing ServingNetwork and unsupported DNN; `releaseSession` records success with its trigger.\r\n  - `context`: `CountSMContextsByState`.\r\n- `go test -race` on the touched packages: clean.\r\n- `golangci-lint run ./...` (repo `.golangci.yml`): no new issues compared with `main` (same 51 pre-existing issues; 61 with per-linter limits off).\r\n- Built the SMF binary with `make smf` from the free5gc superproject.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Example `smfcfg.yaml`\r\n\r\n```yaml\r\nconfiguration:\r\n  # ...\r\n  metrics:\r\n    enable: true          # default false\r\n    scheme: http          # http or https (https needs tls.pem / tls.key)\r\n    bindingIPv4: 127.0.0.2  # may be the SBI IP, but then the port must differ from sbi.port\r\n    port: 9091\r\n    namespace: free5gc    # metric name prefix\r\n```\r\n\r\nExample queries:\r\n\r\n```promql\r\n# Establishment success ratio\r\nsum(rate(free5gc_smf_business_pdu_session_establishment_total{status=\"successful\"}[5m]))\r\n  / sum(rate(free5gc_smf_business_pdu_session_establishment_total[5m]))\r\n\r\n# Failures by cause\r\nsum by (cause) (rate(free5gc_smf_business_pdu_session_establishment_total{status=\"failure\"}[5m]))\r\n\r\n# PFCP timeouts per UPF\r\nsum by (upf, message_type) (rate(free5gc_smf_business_pfcp_request_total{result=\"timeout\"}[5m]))\r\n\r\n# p95 PFCP session establishment latency\r\nhistogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, upf) (\r\n  rate(free5gc_smf_business_pfcp_request_duration_seconds_bucket{message_type=\"session_establishment\"}[5m])))\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Not included (possible follow-ups)\r\n\r\n- Releases triggered by losing a UPF association use their own deletion path, so they aren't in `pdu_session_release_total` (their PFCP deletions are still in `pfcp_request_total`).\r\n- Requests from the UPF to the SMF (Session Report) are not measured.\r\n- No PFCP rejection cause label.\r\n- No per-DNN or per-slice labels.\r\n\r\nRelated: free5gc/free5gc#1176, free5gc/free5gc#1177, free5gc/free5gc#1178, free5gc/free5gc#1179, free5gc/free5gc#1180\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/issues/247/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/smf/issues/247/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":32805163675,"node_id":"SE_lADODiZOqs8AAAABTYDoCM8A